  "imageedit.t26": "Local",
  "imageedit.t27": "— enlarges using the browser’s own 2D interpolation (high quality) only. No API, no network. Detail that was never there will not appear; it just looks less mushy. A super-resolution network like Real-ESRGAN needs a separate model (WASM and such), so it is not included here.",
  "imageedit.t28": "— sends it to Nano Banana, which “guesses” the detail as it enlarges. The request is shrunk to about 1536px on the long edge, and the result is fitted to the scale above.",
